1 ASSEMBLE
    The ASM command assembles VAX source into memory, either from a file
    (ASM file) or, with no file, one statement at a time.  The console accepts
    it only until the microkernel is in place, which is how STARTUP.COM loads
    it (SYS$SOURCES:KERNEL.ASM on the system volume, or govax's built-in
    kernel.asm without one).  After that ASM is a debugger command: enter the
    debugger with DEBUG and type ASM there.  HELP ASM at the DBG> prompt
    describes the assembler, and how its file is found: a volume file or a
    host file, as RUN's is.
